  "description": "COFSEY crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C74 H66 F12 O26 Tb5 1+,C20 H16 F12 O8 Tb1 1-,2(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb5 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb6 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.544-3.600 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.42-100.73°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Tb5(L)4(LH2)2(tfa)4][Tb(tfa)4]·2CH3OH.",
